{
  "protocol_version": 1,
  "description": "File-backed key-value storage vectors for protocol version 1: the layout both implementations' file storage shares. There are no wire vectors. The `file_storage` section holds `key_layout`, which gives for each key the path of the file that holds it or the reason the layout refuses it (an empty key, a NUL, a backslash, a leading slash, an empty, `.` or `..` segment), and `scenarios`, which start from a directory (every file under it as a `/`-joined path with its content in hex), run operations on a storage over a copy of it, and record what each returns and the whole directory after it. A value is the whole content of its file, nothing added. The outcomes are written by hand from the layout, never produced by an implementation.",
